WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.607
It is tempting to think that pivoting and then un pivoting will always return the original data.

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:08.022
That is not true.

00:00:08.022 --> 00:00:15.717
If the pivot aggregated several transaction rows into one total, the individual transactions have already been lost.

00:00:15.717 --> 00:00:23.692
Un pivoting can recover the aggregated product and month totals, but it cannot recreate the original transaction IDs or

00:00:23.692 --> 00:00:25.095
individual amounts.
